---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Install from '../../components/Install.astro';
---

<Doc
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Install just-vibe',
    description: 'One npm package. Your package manager. Your coding agent.',
  }}
>
  <h2>Before you start</h2>
  <p>
    You need <strong>Node.js 22 or newer</strong> and <strong>Codex CLI or Claude Code</strong> with
    native plugin support on your PATH. External workflows use your own service accounts and tools.
  </p>
  <h2>1. Run the installer</h2>
  <p>
    Select your package manager and host, then run this in your terminal. The default target is
    Codex.
  </p>
  <Install id="docs-install" />
  <p>
    The installer copies the bundled plugin into a persistent directory under{' '}
    <code>~/.just-vibe</code> and registers it with the host’s native plugin manager. It survives
    package-manager cache cleanup. The default installation requires no GitHub access.
  </p>
  <h2>2. Start a new conversation</h2>
  <p>In Claude Code, run:</p>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code id="claude-help">/just-vibe:help what is available?</code>
    <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="claude-help" aria-live="polite">
      Copy
    </button>
  </div>
  <p>
    In Codex, select the <strong>help</strong> skill from the just-vibe plugin and add your request.
    The Claude slash syntax is not the Codex skill-picker syntax.
  </p>
  <h2>3. Bring a real task</h2>
  <p>
    Start with <a href="/commands/auto/">auto</a> when you know the outcome you want,{' '}
    <a href="/commands/orient/">orient</a> for an unfamiliar repository, or{' '}
    <a href="/commands/tools/">tools</a> to discover a specific workflow.
  </p>
  <h2>Prefer a project dependency?</h2>
  <p>
    Install the same package locally, then run its CLI. Installing the npm dependency alone does not
    register the plugin.
  </p>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code>
      npm install -D just-vibe
      <br />
      npx just-vibe setup
    </code>
  </div>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code>
      pnpm add -D just-vibe
      <br />
      pnpm exec just-vibe setup
    </code>
  </div>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code>
      yarn add -D just-vibe
      <br />
      yarn just-vibe setup
    </code>
  </div>
  <p>
    Append <code>--target claude</code> to the setup command for Claude Code. Modern Yarn uses{' '}
    <code>yarn dlx</code>; a local dependency is also an option.
  </p>
  <h2>Claude installation scope</h2>
  <p>
    Claude defaults to user scope. From a project directory, use the following for shared project
    enablement. Each teammate still installs their own local marketplace.
  </p>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code>pnpm dlx just-vibe@latest setup --target claude --scope project</code>
  </div>
  <p>
    Use <code>--scope local</code> for unshared project enablement. Keep the same scope for future
    operations. Codex does not take Claude’s scope option.
  </p>
  <h2>Preview before installation</h2>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code>pnpm dlx just-vibe@latest setup --dry-run</code>
  </div>
  <p>
    A dry run does not copy the payload or run host commands. The package manager may still fetch
    and cache the CLI.{' '}
    <a href="/docs/updates/">
      Read about updates and diagnostics <Icon name="arrow-right" />
    </a>
  </p>
</Doc>
